      "sourceText": "[PDF page 77]\n2026-07-23\nNVLINK Debug Flow\nBack to error list\nLast Update: 05/28/2026\nStation: All\nError Description: NVLINK issue (BER, link down, etc)\nComment: NVLINK\nFA Steps\n1. Identify compute tray (CT), switch tray (ST) and cable cartridge (CCB) involved. Use information from error code, station logs, SFC, or mapping\ntool.\n2. Remove CT from rack and inspect\na. Must inspect using fixture and take images of tray and CCB connectors\nb. Review photos\nc. If damage found, replace damaged component and resume testing\nd. If no damage, continue with FA flow\n3. Swap CT with neighbor CT\n4. Retest failing station (run FLC first if necessary)\n5. If failure follows CT to new slot, replace CT with a new one and resume testing\n6. If failure remains on old slot, then proceed to remove and inspect ST\na. Must inspect using fixture and take images of tray and CCB connectors\nb. Review photos\nc. If damage found, replace damaged component and resume testing\nd. If no damage, continue with FA flow\n7. Swap ST with neighbor ST\n8. If failure follows ST to new slot, replace ST with a new one and resume testing\n9. If failure remains in the old slot, replace CCB and resume testing\nSwapping the CT and ST at the same time is allowable as long as inspection is happening of all connectors. It is recommended to proceed with each\nindependently until teams are trained and have proficency in safely swapping trays and identifying connector damage. Flow for swapping both is as\nfollows:\n1. Identify CT, ST and CCB involved.\n2. Remove CT and ST and inspect\na. Must inspect using fixture and take images of both trays and all CCB connectors\nb. Review photos\nc. If damage found, replace damaged component and resume testing\nd. If no damage, continue with FA flow\n3. Swap CT with neighbor CT, swap ST with neigbor ST\n4. Retest\na. If failure follows CT to new slot, replace CT\nb. If failure follows ST to new slot, replace ST\nc. If failure remains on old slots, replace CCB\nReplacing CBC1\nIf CBC1 is replaced after FLB has been run, SWITCH_1 must be factory reset by ssh-ing to the host (nvos) and running:\nnv action reset system factory-default\nNote on CT Replacements\n77 / 80\n\n[PDF page 78]\n2026-07-23\nFor any CT replaced following this process, we must identify the failing bianca (GPU) and report that to L10 for replacement. L10 does not test NVLINK\nso this must be done from the L11 logs.\nFlowchart\nNVLINK FA Flow - Independent Swap\nFound damage Replace damaged\ncomponent\nFound damage\ncom I p d o e n n e t n if t y s : i n C v T o , l v S e T, d CCB a R n e d m i o n v s e p e C c T t Same slot failed a R n e d m i o n v s e p e S c T t\nSame slot failed Replace CCB\nSwap CT with Swap ST with\nNo damage neighbor and No damage neighbor and\nretest retest\nNew slot failed Replace ST\nNew slot failed Replace CT\nInspection Flow\nDamage Tray needs replacement\nInspect tray\nconnectors and Damage CCB needs replacement\ntake photos Inspect CCB\nNo Damage connectors and\ntake photos\nNo Damage Continue testing\nNVLINK FA Flow - Dual Swap\nReplace damaged\nFound damage\ncomponent\nIdentify involved Remove CT and ST,\ncomponents: CT, ST, CCB and inspect Same slots failed Replace CCB\nSwap CT with\nneighbor and\nNo damage CT fails in new slot Replace CT\nswap ST with\nneigbor, retest\nST fails in new slot Replace ST\n78 / 80",
